Young Joe, played by Dante Pereira-Olson.

10
00:46:50,526 --> 00:46:56,526
You Were Never Really Here (released as A Beautiful Day in France and Germany) is a 2017
neo-noir crime psychological thriller film written and directed by Lynne Ramsay.

11
00:51:31,578 --> 00:51:37,578
Based on the 2013 novella of the same name by Jonathan Ames, it stars Joaquin
Phoenix, Ekaterina Samsonov, Alex Manette, John Doman, and Judith Roberts.

12
00:56:12,631 --> 00:56:18,631
In the film, a traumatized mercenary named Joe (Phoenix) is hired by a politician to find and rescue his daughter who has been
kidnapped by a human trafficking network in New York City, which Joe is instructed to destroy by any violent means.

13
01:00:53,684 --> 01:00:59,684
The film was co-produced between the United Kingdom and France.

14
01:05:34,736 --> 01:05:40,736
An early cut premiered at the 2017 Cannes Film Festival in competition, where Ramsay
won the award for Best Screenplay and Phoenix the award for Best Actor.

15
01:10:15,789 --> 01:10:21,789
The film was released by StudioCanal in the UK, on 9 March 2018, and by Amazon Studios in the U.S., where it
began a limited release in Los Angeles and New York on 6 April 2018, and a wide release on 20 April.

16
01:14:56,842 --> 01:15:02,842
It received critical acclaim, with Ramsay's direction and
Phoenix's performance garnering high praise.

17
01:19:37,894 --> 01:19:43,894
The film explores themes of hotel, new york city, post-traumatic stress
disorder (ptsd), based on novel or book, childhood trauma.

18
01:24:18,947 --> 01:24:24,947
The tone is emotional and intense.
